2026-05-28 11:30:34,722 | DEBUG | anthropic._base_client | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2adb9e4a-7f2c-40c0-a0d9-f5fa5f760812', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 8192, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'Requirement (natural language):\nImplement a write-through cache backed by a key-value store.\n\nComponents:\n  1. A backing store mapping keys (from {"a", "b", "c"}) to integer values\n     (in 0..5). Reads return the value or a missing marker; writes overwrite.\n  2. A cache in front of the store with the same key/value domain. On read:\n     return the cache entry if present, else fetch from the store and\n     populate the cache. On write: update both the cache and the store\n     atomically.\n\nSafety properties:\n  - Read-after-write consistency: after Write(k, v), the next Read(k)\n    returns v whether it goes through the cache or directly to the store.\n  - The cache never holds a value for k that disagrees with the store\'s\n    value for k (cache entries are a subset of store entries that match).\n  - The store contains only keys from {"a","b","c"} and values in 0..5.\n\nApproved decomposition plan:\nParent: WriteThroughCacheSystem\nParent role: Composes the cache in front of the backing store, routing Reads and Writes so that writes update both layers atomically and reads populate the cache on miss, while enforcing cache/store agreement.\n\nChild modules:\n  - BackingStore: Persistent key-value store mapping keys in {a,b,c} to integer values in 0..5, with a missing marker for absent keys.\n      state_variables: store\n      actions: StoreRead, StoreWrite\n      invariant_sketch: Store maps only keys in {a,b,c} to values in 0..5 or a missing marker; writes overwrite prior values.\n  - Cache: In-memory cache fronting the store, holding a subset of entries that must agree with the store; supports lookup, populate-on-miss, and invalidation/update.\n      state_variables: cache\n      actions: CacheLookup, CachePopulate, CacheUpdate\n      invariant_sketch: Every cached entry has a key in {a,b,c} and a value in 0..5; cache entries are a subset of store entries with matching values.\n\nPlanner notes: Parent composes BackingStore_Impl and Cache_Impl: Write(k,v) atomically performs CacheUpdate and StoreWrite; Read(k) tries CacheLookup, on miss does StoreRead followed by CachePopulate. Parent-level invariant enforces read-after-write consistency and cache/store agreement across the composed state.\n\nExpand this plan into a ModuleBundle. For each child, emit both <Name>_Abs (pure TLA+) and <Name>_Impl (PlusCal-bearing TLA+). Emit a parent module that INSTANCEs each impl and defines its own composed Inv and Property. Pin small finite CONSTANTS so TLC can model-check exhaustively. Emit one call to propose_module_bundle.'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011UgBcpwBnXm5ABQG1TAMrQ', 'name': 'propose_module_bundle', 'input': {'slug': 'write_through_cache', 'parent': {'name': 'WriteThroughCacheSystem', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'tla_source': '---- MODULE WriteThroughCacheSystem ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, FiniteSets, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\nVARIABLES store, cache, lastOp, lastKey, lastVal, lastReadResult\n\nB == INSTANCE BackingStore_Impl WITH store <- store\nC == INSTANCE Cache_Impl WITH cache <- cache\n\nvars == << store, cache, lastOp, lastKey, lastVal, lastReadResult >>\n\nValidStore(s) == \\A k \\in Keys : s[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\nValidCache(c) == \\A k \\in Keys : c[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nCacheAgreesWithStore ==\n  \\A k \\in Keys : (cache[k] # Missing) => (cache[k] = store[k])\n\nReadAfterWrite ==\n  (lastOp = "ReadAfterWrite") => (lastReadResult = lastVal)\n\nInit ==\n  /\\ store = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing]\n  /\\ cache = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing]\n  /\\ lastOp = "None"\n  /\\ lastKey = CHOOSE k \\in Keys : TRUE\n  /\\ lastVal = CHOOSE v \\in Vals : TRUE\n  /\\ lastReadResult = Missing\n\nWrite(k, v) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ v \\in Vals\n  /\\ store\' = [store EXCEPT ![k] = v]\n  /\\ cache\' = [cache EXCEPT ![k] = v]\n  /\\ lastOp\' = "Write"\n  /\\ lastKey\' = k\n  /\\ lastVal\' = v\n  /\\ lastReadResult\' = Missing\n\nReadHit(k) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ cache[k] # Missing\n  /\\ lastReadResult\' = cache[k]\n  /\\ lastOp\' = IF lastOp = "Write" /\\ lastKey = k THEN "ReadAfterWrite" ELSE "Read"\n  /\\ lastKey\' = k\n  /\\ lastVal\' = cache[k]\n  /\\ UNCHANGED << store, cache >>\n\nReadMiss(k) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ cache[k] = Missing\n  /\\ lastReadResult\' = store[k]\n  /\\ cache\' = [cache EXCEPT ![k] = store[k]]\n  /\\ lastOp\' = IF lastOp = "Write" /\\ lastKey = k THEN "ReadAfterWrite" ELSE "Read"\n  /\\ lastKey\' = k\n  /\\ lastVal\' = IF store[k] = Missing THEN lastVal ELSE store[k]\n  /\\ UNCHANGED store\n\nNext ==\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals : Write(k, v)\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys : ReadHit(k)\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys : ReadMiss(k)\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ ValidStore(store)\n  /\\ ValidCache(cache)\n  /\\ CacheAgreesWithStore\n  /\\ lastOp \\in {"None", "Read", "Write", "ReadAfterWrite"}\n  /\\ lastKey \\in Keys\n  /\\ lastVal \\in Vals\n  /\\ lastReadResult \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n  /\\ ReadAfterWrite\n\nProperty ==\n  /\\ CacheAgreesWithStore\n  /\\ ReadAfterWrite\n====\n'}, 'modules': [{'name': 'BackingStore', 'role': 'abs', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'constants': {'values': {'Keys': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'Vals': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'Missing': ['NONE']}}, 'tla_source': "---- MODULE BackingStore_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\nVARIABLES store\n\nvars == << store >>\n\nValidStore(s) == \\A k \\in Keys : s[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInit == store = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing]\n\nStoreWrite(k, v) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ v \\in Vals\n  /\\ store' = [store EXCEPT ![k] = v]\n\nStoreReadStep ==\n  /\\ UNCHANGED store\n\nNext ==\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals : StoreWrite(k, v)\n  \\/ StoreReadStep\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == ValidStore(store)\n\nProperty == ValidStore(store)\n====\n"}, {'name': 'BackingStore', 'role': 'impl', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'constants': {'values': {'Keys': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'Vals': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'Missing': ['NONE']}}, 'abstraction_map': {'store': 'store'}, 'tla_source': '---- MODULE BackingStore_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\n(* --algorithm BackingStore\nvariables\n  store = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing];\n\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals do\n          store[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        skip;\n      end either;\n    end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nValidStore(s) == \\A k \\in Keys : s[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ ValidStore(store)\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop"}\n\nProperty == ValidStore(store)\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE BackingStore_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\n(* --algorithm BackingStore\nvariables\n  store = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing];\n\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals do\n          store[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        skip;\n      end either;\n    end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nValidStore(s) == \\A k \\in Keys : s[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ ValidStore(store)\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop"}\n\nProperty == ValidStore(store)\n====\n'}, {'name': 'Cache', 'role': 'abs', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'constants': {'values': {'Keys': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'Vals': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'Missing': ['NONE']}}, 'tla_source': "---- MODULE Cache_Abs ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\nVARIABLES cache\n\nvars == << cache >>\n\nValidCache(c) == \\A k \\in Keys : c[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInit == cache = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing]\n\nCacheUpdate(k, v) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ v \\in Vals\n  /\\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![k] = v]\n\nCachePopulate(k, v) ==\n  /\\ k \\in Keys\n  /\\ v \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n  /\\ cache' = [cache EXCEPT ![k] = v]\n\nCacheLookupStep ==\n  /\\ UNCHANGED cache\n\nNext ==\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals : CacheUpdate(k, v)\n  \\/ \\E k \\in Keys, v \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing}) : CachePopulate(k, v)\n  \\/ CacheLookupStep\n\nSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_vars\n\nInv == ValidCache(cache)\n\nProperty == ValidCache(cache)\n====\n"}, {'name': 'Cache', 'role': 'impl', 'invariant_name': 'Inv', 'property_name': 'Property', 'constants': {'values': {'Keys': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'Vals': [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 'Missing': ['NONE']}}, 'abstraction_map': {'cache': 'cache'}, 'tla_source': '---- MODULE Cache_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\n(* --algorithm Cache\nvariables\n  cache = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing];\n\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals do\n          cache[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing}) do\n          cache[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        skip;\n      end either;\n    end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nValidCache(c) == \\A k \\in Keys : c[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ ValidCache(cache)\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop"}\n\nProperty == ValidCache(cache)\n====\n', 'pluscal_source': '---- MODULE Cache_Impl ----\nEXTENDS Naturals, TLC\n\nCONSTANTS Keys, Vals, Missing\n\n(* --algorithm Cache\nvariables\n  cache = [k \\in Keys |-> Missing];\n\nbegin\n  Loop:\n    while TRUE do\n      either\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in Vals do\n          cache[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        with k \\in Keys, v \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing}) do\n          cache[k] := v;\n        end with;\n      or\n        skip;\n      end either;\n    end while;\nend algorithm; *)\n\nValidCache(c) == \\A k \\in Keys : c[k] \\in (Vals \\cup {Missing})\n\nInv ==\n  /\\ ValidCache(cache)\n  /\\ pc \\in {"Loop"}\n\nProperty == ValidCache(cache)\n====\n'}]}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011UgBcpwBnXm5ABQG1TAMrQ', 'content': "The bundle failed model checking. Details:\n\nTOOLCHAIN ERRORS (fix these FIRST — TLC cannot run until they're cleared):\n- BackingStore: SANY: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- Cache: SANY: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- refinement: SANY: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n\n- module BackingStore :: init: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\nFirst error line: Parsing or semantic analysis failed.\n- module BackingStore :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module BackingStore :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\nFirst error line: Parsing or semantic analysis failed.\n- module Cache :: init: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Cache :: consec: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- module Cache :: property: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n- refinement obligation: ERROR\n    note: TLC exited with a non-zero code but no recognisable invariant or initial-predicate violation was found in its output. This usually means a parse/semantic error in the spec or config.\n\nLast bundle slug: write_through_cache\nParent module: WriteThroughCacheSystem\nModules: BackingStore(abs), BackingStore(impl), Cache(abs), Cache(impl)\nRevise the failing module(s) and/or abstraction map(s). Return one call to repair_module_bundle with the FULL revised bundle."}]}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-7', 'system': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are repairing a multi-module ModuleBundle that failed one or more proof\nobligations under TLC. The user message lists each failing obligation: it\nmay be a per-impl (Init/Consec/Property) failure, or the cross-module\nrefinement obligation.\n\nYour task\n---------\nDiagnose the failures and emit a revised bundle via the\n`repair_module_bundle` tool. Set `targeted_failure` to point at the most\nimportant failure (e.g. `"Queue/consec"`, `"refinement"`, `"parent/property"`).\nProvide a brief `reasoning`.\n\nDiagnosis guidance\n------------------\n* Per-impl `init`/`consec`/`property` failures behave exactly like the\n  single-module flow: weaken or strengthen `Inv`, or fix the algorithm.\n* `refinement` failure: the impl\'s abstraction_map is wrong (e.g. it\n  projects onto a state that does NOT correspond to a valid Abs state) OR\n  the impl does something the Abs cannot simulate. Either fix the map or\n  restrict the impl.\n* Parent failures: the parent\'s composed `Inv` does not hold, or fails to\n  imply the parent\'s `Property`. Strengthen the composed `Inv`, possibly\n  pulling in an additional impl invariant via INSTANCE projection.\n\nOutput rules\n------------\nRe-emit the WHOLE bundle (parent + every module), even unchanged ones, so\nthe verifier can re-run cleanly. Do not respond with prose; call\n`repair_module_bundle` exactly once.\n', 'cache_control': {'type': 'ephemeral'}}], 'tool_choice': {'type': 'tool', 'name': 'repair_module_bundle'}, 'tools': [{'name': 'repair_module_bundle', 'description': "Emit a revised ModuleBundle after one or more proof obligations failed (a per-impl Init/Consec/Property, or the refinement obligation across all impls). Diagnose whether a specific module's Inv was too weak/strong, its PlusCal is wrong, its abstraction_map is wrong, or the parent's composed Inv/Property is wrong, and revise accordingly.", 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['reasoning', 'targeted_failure', 'slug', 'parent', 'modules'], 'properties': {'reasoning': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Brief diagnosis of which obligation failed and what changed.'}, 'targeted_failure': {'type': 'string', 'description': "Free-form pointer at the failure: a module name + obligation ('Queue/consec'), or 'refinement', or 'parent/property'."}, 'slug': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[a-z][a-z0-9_]*$'}, 'parent': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['name', 'tla_source'], 'properties': {'name': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$', 'description': 'Parent module name (matches plan.parent_name).'}, 'tla_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Full TLA+ module source for the parent: `---- MODULE <Name> ----` that EXTENDS / INSTANCEs each <Child>_Impl and defines composed Inv and Property. No PlusCal block here — composition lives purely at the TLA+ layer.'}, 'constants': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Finite domains for TLA+ CONSTANTS. Each key is a CONSTANT name; each value is a list of allowed values (small finite domains keep TLC tractable).', 'properties': {'values': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': ['string', 'integer']}, 'minItems': 1}}}, 'required': ['values']}, 'invariant_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Inv'}, 'property_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Property'}}}, 'modules': {'type': 'array', 'minItems': 2, 'maxItems': 8, 'items': {'type': 'object', 'required': ['name', 'role', 'tla_source'], 'properties': {'name': {'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$', 'description': 'Conceptual module name from the plan; final file names are <name>_Abs.tla / <name>_Impl.tla.'}, 'role': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['abs', 'impl'], 'description': "'abs' = abstract contract (pure TLA+ Spec / Inv). 'impl' = concrete implementation containing a PlusCal block."}, 'tla_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Full TLA+ module source: `---- MODULE <Name>_Abs ----` or `---- MODULE <Name>_Impl ----`. For impls, this must contain a `(* --algorithm <Name> ... *)` block; pcal.trans will rewrite the file in place. Do NOT pre-insert `\\* BEGIN TRANSLATION`.'}, 'pluscal_source': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'For impl modules only: same text as `tla_source`. The verifier uses presence of this field as a flag to call pcal.trans. Leave unset for abs modules.'}, 'constants': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Finite domains for TLA+ CONSTANTS. Each key is a CONSTANT name; each value is a list of allowed values (small finite domains keep TLC tractable).', 'properties': {'values': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': ['string', 'integer']}, 'minItems': 1}}}, 'required': ['values']}, 'abstraction_map': {'type': 'object', 'description': "For impl modules only: maps each variable of the sibling <Name>_Abs module to a TLA+ expression. Expressions MUST be in terms of the parent's own VARIABLES (the bare names declared in the parent module), NOT the '<Alias>!var' form. TLA+'s M!x accessor works only for defined operators of M, not for its variables — SANY/TLC reject '<Alias>!var' references with 'Unknown operator: var'. The parent's '<Alias> == INSTANCE <Name>_Impl WITH <impl_var> <- <parent_var>' has already bound impl variables to parent variables, and the refinement aux module EXTENDS the parent so those parent variables are in scope. Example: given Queue_Abs.queue and a parent variable 'buffer', write {'queue': 'buffer'}.", 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'string'}, 'default': {}}, 'invariant_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Inv'}, 'property_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Property'}}}}, 'notes': {'type': 'string', 'default': ''}}}}]}}
