re names declared in the parent module), NOT the '<Alias>!var' form. TLA+'s M!x accessor works only for defined operators of M, not for its variables — SANY/TLC reject '<Alias>!var' references with 'Unknown operator: var'. The parent's '<Alias> == INSTANCE <Name>_Impl WITH <impl_var> <- <parent_var>' has already bound impl variables to parent variables, and the refinement aux module EXTENDS the parent so those parent variables are in scope. Example: given Queue_Abs.queue and a parent variable 'buffer', write {'queue': 'buffer'}.", 'additionalProperties': {'type': 'string'}, 'default': {}}, 'invariant_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Inv'}, 'property_name': {'type': 'string', 'default': 'Property'}}}}, 'notes': {'type': 'string', 'default': ''}}}}]}}
